<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!--
    The type tokens (T-155): the ramp the host views set their text by.
    Four steps only — Caption 11 / Body 13 / SubtitleStrong 14 / Title 16 —
    and the platform default (Avalonia's TextElement default of 12) is the
    implicit control-text step the ramp documents but does not republish:
    an unset FontSize IS 12, so the host views carry no 12 literal at all.
    These are static design constants (a theme switch retints colors, it
    never resizes type), so consumers read them with StaticResource.
    -->

    <x:Double x:Key="CaptionFontSize">11</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="BodyFontSize">13</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="SubtitleStrongFontSize">14</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="TitleFontSize">16</x:Double>

    <!--
    The spacing scale (T-155): 4 / 8 / 12 / 16 / 24. Two shapes of the same
    scale — the raw steps are doubles for the Spacing family (StackPanel
    Spacing, Grid Row/ColumnSpacing), the insets are uniform Thickness for
    Margin and Padding. A value between the steps is a layout-tuning
    decision, not a scale member: the host surfaces adopting the scale ride
    only these five steps.
    -->

    <x:Double x:Key="SpaceXs">4</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="SpaceS">8</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="SpaceM">12</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="SpaceL">16</x:Double>
    <x:Double x:Key="SpaceXl">24</x:Double>

    <Thickness x:Key="InsetXs">4</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="InsetS">8</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="InsetM">12</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="InsetL">16</Thickness>
    <Thickness x:Key="InsetXl">24</Thickness>

    <!--
    The numeric stack (T-155): the tabular numerals. Numeric surfaces —
    the stats tiles, the table columns, the price fields — set digits in a
    monospaced face so the columns hold their place across rows, themes and
    languages (the HUD's precedent, now a token the whole app shares).
    -->

    <FontFamily x:Key="NumericFont">Consolas,Menlo,DejaVu Sans Mono,monospace</FontFamily>

</ResourceDictionary>
